🎯 What this agent does
Given a goal like:
	“Investigate high CPU usage”
The agent will:
	1. Decide what to check
	2. Run Linux commands (top, ps, vmstat, etc.)
	3. Observe output
	4. Reason
	5. Suggest fixes

🧱 STEP 1: System Requirements
✔ Python 3.10+
✔ Linux / macOS
✔ Ollama installed and running

Check Ollama

ollama --version
Pull model

ollama pull llama3



📦 STEP 2: Create Virtual Environment (Recommended)

python3 -m venv agentenv
source agentenv/bin/activate



📦 STEP 3: Install Dependencies

pip install langchain langchain-community langchain-core
Verify:

pip list | grep langchain


📁 STEP 4: Project Structure

devops-agent/
│
├── devops_agent.py
└── README.md (optional)


🧠 STEP 5: FULL RUNNABLE SCRIPT
📄 File: devops_agent.py
================================================
📄 File: devops_agent.py
command_policy.py --> allowed and not allowed commands
requirements.txt --> packages required

=========================================================


▶️ STEP 6: Run the Agent
python devops_agent.py

Example input:
Investigate high CPU usage on this system


🔒 STEP 7: Safety Features Included

✅ Command blocking
✅ Timeout
✅ Read-only inspection
❌ No destructive commands


🧠 STEP 8: Try More Goals

Check disk IO latency
Why is memory usage increasing?
Analyze load average
Find top 5 memory consuming processes
Explain vmstat output


